From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 09:21:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: file-based backup export/import

- tar streaming via vendored astral-tokio-tar fork whose tokio dep is
  the tokio-wasm-shim facade (memfs-backed fs on wasm)
- Sql::import wasm variant: sqlite-wasm-rs has no sqlcipher_export, so
  close the pool and swap the DB file bytes in the VFS instead
  (encrypted backups stay unsupported on wasm)
- scheduler stop: TaskTracker/timeout path cfg-gated for wasm
- delete_file routes through the memfs shim

wasm: VFS-agnostic sqlite backup import/export

The backup DB swap was hardwired to MemVfsUtil; with the OPFS sahpool
VFS as default it silently targeted the wrong VFS. Route through the
shim's sqlite_vfs_import/take, which dispatch to whichever VFS is
default.

Since v2.64.0: export_database() lost its timestamp argument and no
longer writes backup_time upstream (1721c0316); the wasm variant
follows. Scheduler::stop() now aborts a task that misses the 30s
shutdown timeout (#8832); the sequential wasm path does the same.
